# Sanitizer special-case list, configured and applied by Sanitizers.cmake whenever SANITIZE is set.
#
# Vendored third-party code is excluded from instrumentation-time checks because we cannot fix what it reports without
# diverging from upstream, and a finding we will never act on is worse than no finding: it trains the reader to scroll
# past a sanitizer block that might, next time, be ours.
#
# stb_image_write.h's JPEG encoder is the current occupant, shifting a value out of int's range in its bit packer.
#
# This silences reports ATTRIBUTED to these files only. Our own code stays fully instrumented, including the calls it
# makes into these libraries, so a bad pointer or size we hand them is still caught here.
# Anchored to this repository's root: as a consumer's submodule, shaped-core itself sits under that consumer's extern/,
# and a bare */extern/* would exclude all of shaped-core there.
# A consumer excludes its own vendored code with an ignorelist of its own.
src:@SC_SANITIZER_ROOT@/extern/*
